Initialize RandR's shared state before registering its client callback.

Xnest does not call RRScreenInit(), so rrPrivKeyRec is never registered
through RRInit(). Initializing the extension nevertheless makes the first
client connection assert in RRClientCallback() when it looks up the
screen private. Call RRInit() here as well; it is safe to repeat within
a server generation and also initializes the RandR resource types.

This preserves extension initialization without RandR-enabled screens.

Upstream report:
https://github.com/XQuartz/XQuartz/issues/517

Regression introduced by:
https://github.com/XQuartz/xorg-server/commit/535a649c0b7d2a1cf2ed5c3d41a78502c4f217d3

--- a/randr/randr.c
+++ b/randr/randr.c
@@ -414,6 +414,9 @@ RRExtensionInit(void)
 {
     ExtensionEntry *extEntry;

+    if (!RRInit())
+        return;
+
     if (!dixRegisterPrivateKey(&RRClientPrivateKeyRec, PRIVATE_CLIENT,
                                sizeof(RRClientRec) +
                                screenInfo.numScreens * sizeof(RRTimesRec)))
